---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'August 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description={`Cookie policy for ${SITE.name}.`} lang="en">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies (and similar technologies like local storage) are small pieces of data a website can
        store in your browser, usually to remember something between visits — a preference, a login
        session, or in our case, whether you've responded to the cookie banner.
      </p>

      <h2>Always active — no consent needed</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>terminal41-cookie-consent</code></td>
            <td>Local storage (not a cookie)</td>
            <td>Remembers whether you accepted or declined the cookie banner</td>
            <td>Until you clear your browser data</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>This one is strictly functional — it's what makes the banner not reappear on every page.</p>

      <h2>Only active if you click "Accept"</h2>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand which guides get read and how people
        find the site. It only starts running after you click "Accept" on the cookie banner —
        if you decline, or haven't made a choice yet, none of the cookies below are set.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Provider</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>_ga</code></td>
            <td>Google Analytics</td>
            <td>Distinguishes unique visitors</td>
            <td>~2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code></td>
            <td>Google Analytics</td>
            <td>Persists session state for the GA4 property</td>
            <td>~2 years</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Google's own use of this data is governed by the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
        You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking across all sites using Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">browser add-on</a>,
        or simply click "Decline" on our banner.
      </p>

      <h2>Managing your choice</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your mind at any time by clearing your browser's local storage for this site,
        which will bring the cookie banner back on your next visit. Most browsers also let you block
        or delete cookies and local storage entirely through their privacy settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
